1. The on-device agent has begun being ported to a Rockchip development board. Optimization is ongoing, and several issues have been resolved. The Qwen-VL-4B model was re-exported and appears to be useful based on the current results. However, the export still has issues, so it needs to be re-exported.

2. Graphiti has been introduced as the external memory system for the on-device agent. A dedicated evaluation system for the memory components has been mostly completed. However, each evaluation run currently takes several days, so we need to investigate ways to reduce the runtime.

3. Qwen3-ASR-1.7B was exported for the Rockchip development board. It has not been optimized yet; the main purpose was to demonstrate its performance to Nissan.
